export const INITIAL_MANUSCRIPT = "# THE PAPER TRAIL\n\n## Reconstructed Master Production Manuscript — V4 · Proposed Full Draft\n\n**Host and narrator:** Logan Black  \n**Format:** Single, audio-only investigative documentary  \n**Editorial status:** Complete proposed narrative draft; original manuscript remains unchanged  \n**Production status:** Transcript-based. Original audio has not been auditioned in this workspace; exact cut points, speaker tone, and room-tone transitions are subject to audio assembly. The archival windows below are source recording positions, *not* episode running times. Written messages are read by Logan, never presented as original audio. Where a compiled source has no reliable absolute date, the manuscript does not invent one.  \n**Editorial rule:** The public accusations heard in the opening are Angela's allegations. Their inclusion does not establish that the alleged conduct occurred. The July 15 private message is attributed to Angela on the basis of the producer's confirmed correction of a speaker-label error in the available transcript.\n\n---\n\n# PROLOGUE — THE THINGS SHE SAID\n\n[START ON ARCHIVAL ROOM SOUND. NO TITLE MUSIC. NO INTRODUCTORY NARRATION. USE REAL SOURCE TEXTURES; MAKE EACH CUT AUDIBLE AS A CHANGE OF ROOM. DO NOT STACK OR OVERLAP VOICES.]\n\n[ARCHIVAL 01 — ANGELA | *Petty Space*, September 8, 2026 | `Petty_Space_-_Addressing_the_Men_Who_Provoked_Me_With_My_Dead_Baby_transcript (2).txt` | source window **00:04–00:42**]\n\n> Fuck you, Logan, and fuck you, Orr. You're trash for talking about my dead baby.\n\n[HARD CUT.]\n\n[ARCHIVAL 02 — ANGELA | *Logan Black Unmasked*, September 18, 2026 | `LOGAN_BLACK_UNMASKED_-_WEAPONIZING_WOMEN_ON_UFO_X_transcript (3).txt` | source window **01:00–04:33**]\n\n> The issue that you have with me is that I called you out for making my friend, who I've known for a year and a half before you ever started dating her, suicidal.\n\n[HARD CUT.]\n\n[ARCHIVAL 03 — ANGELA | *Hook Line Sinker*, September 8, 2026 | `Hook_Line_Sinker_-_How_Psychological_Operations_Reel_Us_In_transcript (2).txt` | source window **00:53–09:08**. The preceding audio establishes that Angela is addressing Logan.]\n\n> I have the AI porn videos that you've been making. All these different women's nudes that you've collected.\n\n[HARD CUT.]\n\n[ARCHIVAL 04 — ANGELA | *Logan Black Unmasked*, September 18, 2026 | same original transcript as ARCHIVAL 02 | source window **01:00–04:33**]\n\n> I didn't call you a fucking pedophile. I called you a predator because that is what you are. The behavior is predatory.\n\n[ONE BREATH OF ROOM TONE.]\n\n[ARCHIVAL 05 — ANGELA | *Petty Space*, September 8, 2026 | source window **11:45–15:10**]\n\n> And so if he wants to paint me as the big bad wolf, I'll share every fucking DM we've ever talked about going all the way back to 2023 in the Discord. And even the ones where you've edited your messages. Because like I told you, I screenshot in real time.\n\n[HARD CUT TO THE EARLIER PORTION OF THE SAME SEPTEMBER 8 BROADCAST; CLEARLY AN EDIT TO A DIFFERENT POINT IN THAT SHOW.]\n\n[ARCHIVAL 06 — ANGELA | *Petty Space*, September 8, 2026 | source window **01:53–02:21**]\n\n> Alright, here's the next four screenshots posted down below. We're gonna do it in increments of four. After I post all these screenshots, then we will talk about it. I just wanna make sure to get this all on the record before, um... Somebody cries in my DM to not share them anymore. And I don't give a fuck. I'm just gonna share them.\n\n[CUT THE SOURCE CLEANLY. COMPLETE SILENCE. APPROXIMATELY TWO SECONDS.]\n\n[ARCHIVAL 07 — ANGELA, A DIFFERENT DELIVERY | *Hook Line Sinker*, September 8, 2026 | `Hook_Line_Sinker_-_How_Psychological_Operations_Reel_Us_In_transcript (2).txt` | source window **55:03–57:47**]\n\n> So Logan was the second space I've ever told my story in. He was like the third friend I made on here.\n\n[EDIT — LATER IN THE SAME ANSWER; KEEP THE CUT AUDIBLE.]\n\n> So I established a friendship with him. He had helped me get information about my family and the back channels. And so I defended him relentlessly.\n\n[LET HER LAST WORD END. NO MUSIC UNDER IT.]\n\n[LOGAN — NARRATION]\n\nThat was Angela Maggard. And the Logan she's talking about is me.\n\nIf you're hearing this for the first time, I know how it sounds. The first group of recordings comes from Angela talking about somebody she says is a predator. Somebody she says has been collecting and sharing intimate images. Somebody she says hurt her friend. Those are serious accusations. I dispute them. And we're going to look at the material behind some of them, because what actually happened matters.\n\nBut that's not where the story starts.\n\nThe second recording is Angela describing our friendship. And that part is real. I helped her. I defended her. She came into my rooms, told me she was going through something terrible, and I believed her.\n\nWhat I couldn't have imagined then was hearing my name in broadcasts like the ones you just heard. Or that conversations shared in confidence would become part of the show.\n\nAnd this didn't happen just to me. There were other people who believed they were helping Angela. People who barely knew each other, who eventually found themselves asking versions of the same question: what happens to the things you tell someone when they stop seeing you as a friend?\n\n[THE PAPER TRAIL SONIC MOTIF — BRIEF, ORIGINAL AND RESTRAINED: THREE SPACED, DRY NOTES; A LOW, CLOSE TEXTURAL PULSE THAT RECEDES RATHER THAN SWELLS.]\n\nI'm Logan Black. This is **The Paper Trail**.\n\n[MOTIF RESOLVES. DRY NARRATION RESUMES.]\n\n---\n\n# CHAPTER ONE — WHY WE BELIEVED HER\n\n[LOGAN — NARRATION]\n\nTo understand any of this, you need to understand the place where we met.\n\nOn X, formerly Twitter, there's a network of people who spend hours talking in live audio rooms called Spaces. People drop in, sit on the stage, pass the microphone around. Some come for the UFO stories, some for government secrets, some to argue. People talk about everything: intelligence agencies, childhood experiences, whether the government knows more than it's saying.\n\nAnd after a while, it's not just the topics anymore. The same voices keep showing up. You learn who's funny. Who argues with everyone. Who needs help. You move into private messages. Maybe you talk off-platform. Before you know it, someone you've never sat in a room with in person feels like part of your daily life.\n\nAngela entered those rooms describing herself as a whistleblower. She spoke about childhood abuse, trafficking allegations involving her family. What she believed were efforts to prevent her story from reaching the public. I can't establish every claim in that history from this episode's material, and the point here isn't to adjudicate her childhood. It's what happened when people responded to the person presenting that story.\n\n[ARCHIVAL 08 — ANGELA | *Hook Line Sinker*, September 8, 2026 | existing V3 locator: `20260908_1nGeLMjONkAKX.json`, `/segments/32`, **2446.72–2562.16 seconds**]\n\n> I'm a whistleblower who came here to share truth. And dealt with psychological operations. Trying to hinder and silence my story from ever going mainstream.\n\n[LOGAN]\n\nThat was the Angela I met: someone who said she was being targeted and needed to be heard. I had a microphone. I had people listening. So I gave her a place to speak. When she needed help researching her family's history, I helped with that too. I even worked on a website mock-up to organize the material she wanted to present.\n\nI wasn't doing it because she was paying me. I didn't have some elaborate arrangement with her. I thought I was helping someone tell her story.\n\nAnd there were people who genuinely appreciated what Angela did for them.\n\n[ARCHIVAL 09 — URS, PARTICIPANT | *Super Spy Tea Time Red String Therapy, Part 4*, September 15, 2026 | existing V3 locator: `20260915_1qGvvebNOARGB.json`, `/segments/158`, **6326.45–6431.05 seconds**]\n\n> Angela has defended me before. There was a bully that said a lot of shit. Was it like two years ago? And she exposed him on X.\n\n[EDIT — LATER IN SAME TURN.]\n\n> So, you know, I just really want to thank you, Angela.\n\n[LOGAN]\n\nI want you to hear that appreciation without immediately putting a sinister spin on it. A person says Angela defended him against somebody he thought was a bully. He thanks her. That's how trust gets built. You believe someone will stand up for you, and you want to stand up for them.\n\nAnd I know what that feels like, because I did it.\n\nBut there's a second part to this story, and it's something I didn't think much about when our friendship was intact. Angela was keeping records. Not just of people she believed were attacking her. Of conversations happening around her—sometimes with people who thought they were still on good terms.\n\nThe first time I can put you in the room for that, I'm there too.\n\n---\n\n# CHAPTER TWO — RAINY DAY\n\n[NO MUSIC. LET THE ORIGINAL AFTERSPACE ROOM NOISE ESTABLISH ITSELF BEFORE THE SPEECH.]\n\n[LOGAN]\n\nFebruary 18, 2026. A late-night X Space. Angela was talking about one of the disputes she was involved in. I came up to speak, and I thanked her.\n\n[ARCHIVAL 10 — LOGAN | *Afterspace*, February 18, 2026 | `20260218_1ZkKzjngDnaKv.json`, `/segments/846`, **13356.70–13364.05 seconds**]\n\n> I appreciate everything you've said, Angela.\n\n[ARCHIVAL 11 — ANGELA, CONTINUOUS SOURCE HANDOFF | *Afterspace*, February 18, 2026 | same source, `/segments/847`, **13365.15–13369.33 seconds**]\n\n> There's way more screenshots than that. I'm just keeping them for a rainy day.\n\n[BRIEF SILENCE.]\n\n[LOGAN]\n\nI remember the situation differently now than I understood it that night. When she said that, I wasn't thinking about myself. I was her friend. The screenshots seemed to be about someone else. In these rooms, everybody talks about receipts. People save messages because other people deny saying things. Sometimes those records really do settle an argument.\n\nSo the phrase didn't set off an alarm in my head. It was just another remark during another late-night conversation.\n\nBut now, knowing what came later, I hear something else in it. Not proof of a plan to target me. That's not what she said. I hear how ordinary it had become for all of us to accept a private archive sitting quietly in the background.\n\nAngela made that practice explicit in other broadcasts.\n\n[ARCHIVAL 12 — ANGELA | *Oor Brought a Chipper, Survivors Brought Receipts*, September 13, 2026 | original transcript `Oor_Brought_a_Chipper__Survivors_Brought_Receipts__transcript (4).txt`; V3 locator `20260913_1lJQRWAWpvVxE.json`, `/segments/24`, **750.71–794.31 seconds**]\n\n> I still care. But I'm still taking notes the whole fucking time. Because I want to see how far you're going to go. And I hate being right. And that's the great thing about writing everything down every single fucking day. You have a timeline.\n\n[LOGAN]\n\nThere's a difference between saving a message because somebody might lie about it, and quietly preparing for the moment when a person you still call a friend becomes an opponent. Angela's words don't establish what she planned to do with every note. They do tell us she could be documenting a relationship while she still cared about the person in it.\n\nAnd privacy settings? She had her own approach to those.\n\n[ARCHIVAL 13 — ANGELA | *Uncensored Truth — Not Your Therapist*, September 6, 2026 | `Uncensored_Truth_Not_Your_Therapist_-_Angela_and_SaraBeth_Truth_Hour_transcript.txt`; V3 locator `20260906_1nGnRBnpYdXGO.json`, `/segments/143`, **5173.65–5301.41 seconds**]\n\n> I don't care about these settings. You can put it in the group chat. You can't screenshot shit. I got a separate phone. I'm gonna just record it either way\n\n[LOGAN]\n\nThat's not me guessing how she obtained a screenshot. That's Angela describing a workaround for a chat's own restrictions. It matters because a person may assume that a conversation is staying in one place when somebody else has already decided to keep a copy.\n\nShe also talked about getting a view of rooms she wasn't in.\n\n[ARCHIVAL 14 — ANGELA | *Logan Black Unmasked*, September 18, 2026 | source window **01:52:22–01:52:32**]\n\n> See, the one thing I like to do is I'll send people in the community that I know in real life to watch you talk shit about me so I can see both sides, and then I'll play dumb. I'll do that for months.\n\n[LOGAN]\n\nListen, a lot of people in this community document arguments. I have too. This isn't a story about how nobody should ever save a conversation. Some of the very recordings you're hearing are important precisely because they were preserved.\n\nThe difference appears when somebody starts talking about using those records to pressure someone else. And there is a public exchange in which Angela is confronted about exactly that.\n\nThe woman asking the questions is named Lynn.\n\n---\n\n# CHAPTER THREE — LYNN DOESN'T WANT A WAR\n\n[LOGAN]\n\nBefore the confrontation, there's something you should know about Lynn. She had supported people financially in this community, sometimes just because she liked what they were doing. She didn't describe it as an investment. She said helping people made her happy.\n\n[ARCHIVAL 15 — LYNN / \"LINN\" IN TRANSCRIPT | *Who or What has Ruined UFO X Spaces*, original transcript title `Who_or_What_has_Ruined_UFO_X_Spaces_transcript (1).txt`; V3 source line 1317, window **01:44:35–01:47:02**]\n\n> Sometimes I just like, I send it. I just send it and it just gives me joy, even if it has put me in a bad position or has Released my information to people that have used it against me. I won't feel guilty about it because I still believe that it came from a good place and I know what I'm doing, and I do believe the best in people.\n\n[LOGAN]\n\nOne of the people Lynn supported was a host named Oor. You don't need to know every argument Oor has had to understand why that mattered. Angela regarded him as someone who had threatened or harassed women. Lynn says she was supporting somebody whose broadcasts she liked. Angela saw the financial support differently.\n\nThat's the disagreement. But when Lynn and Angela found themselves speaking in the same public room, Lynn had another problem: her name had appeared in Angela's newsletter, and she wanted to know why.\n\n[ARCHIVAL 16 — CONTINUOUS EXCHANGE, ANGELA / LYNN / OTHER PARTICIPANT | *Who or What has Ruined UFO X Spaces* | V3 source lines 601–629, broad **46:34–48:03**. Preserve crosstalk and original order; excerpt only at verified source edit points.]\n\n> **Angela:** I never went after you. I just told you that I didn't want anything to do with you because you were funding and giving money to individuals that were harassing and threatening women.\n>\n> **Lynn:** You put me in your newsletter, Angela. You want everything to do with me.\n>\n> **Angela:** With all due respect though, like, I've gone through a lot of crap for 4 and a half years.\n>\n> **Lynn:** I don't even know you.\n>\n> **Angela:** I didn't deserve half of the shit, but you platformed that man knowing that he was threatening to rape and murder people. My voice was stolen only because I didn't agree with people that used to be my friends. I sat where you sat. They weaponized me to do this, and I get— I get it. I've been in your shoes, so I'm not angry at you for that. I blocked you for my peace of mind because I'm super tired of getting screen recordings and screenshots of, oh, this girl's talking crap, this girl's paying this person to target you. It's just happening every damn day, so I blocked all of y'all.\n>\n> **Lynn:** Angela, that's not fair. You blocked me because you thought I had a space when you were having a space, and you said, I'm blocking you, bitch. You said this a couple months ago, and I was like, why?\n>\n> **Angela:** And I blocked you and I unblocked you, did I not? I unblocked you.\n>\n> **Lynn:** And then— and then you said—\n>\n> **Angela:** and then you said You're—\n>\n> **Lynn:** you, you accuse me of being some sort of, um, predator sympathizer or something.\n>\n> **Another participant:** Supporter.\n>\n> **Angela:** Predator supporter.\n>\n> **Lynn:** And you're— and now, and just yesterday or 2 days ago, I was sent some sort of newsletter you have me in. So, Angela, you know, in, in good faith, honestly, can you just— can we just, like, have a truce of some sorts?\n>\n> **Angela:** I would like to have basic communication, but the fact is my voice has been stolen from every single space for 2 weeks now. I'm a little riled up.\n>\n> **Lynn:** I didn't steal it though, Angela.\n\n[LET LYNN FINISH. NO NARRATION FOR ONE BEAT.]\n\n[LOGAN]\n\nThey're not even having the same conversation. Lynn is trying to settle a dispute that has begun to affect her own life. Angela is talking about a larger campaign against her, one she believes involves people who platform her enemies. She isn't simply saying Lynn and Oor have different opinions. She's linking Lynn's financial choices to alleged harassment of women.\n\nAnd the disagreement gets sharper. About fifteen minutes later, Angela refers to the amounts Lynn has been giving people and tells her she's collecting the information.\n\n[ARCHIVAL 17 — EDITED EXCHANGE, ANGELA / LYNN | *Who or What has Ruined UFO X Spaces* | V3 source lines 811–831, broad **01:01:33–01:02:40**. Two discontinuities must be visibly marked in production and audibly clean.]\n\n> **Angela:** I'm not here to sit here with people that platform predators. You're trying to steal my fucking voice, and all you're doing is paying the people that are harassing me. That's what I've been collecting.\n>\n> **Lynn:** I'm not paying anybody to harass you at all.\n>\n> **Angela:** How much money have you been giving to these people? Because that's going to be in my discovery.\n>\n> **Angela:** I have receipts.\n\n[EDIT — MOVE FORWARD TO LYNN AT 01:02:32; DO NOT PRESENT AS ONE UNBROKEN SENTENCE.]\n\n> **Lynn:** Post them, Angela.\n\n[EDIT — MOVE FORWARD TO ANGELA AT 01:02:37.]\n\n> **Angela:** It's going to be your fault that I'm posting them.\n>\n> **Lynn:** Go ahead, Angela.\n\n[NO MUSIC.]\n\n[LOGAN]\n\nThat is the sentence I keep coming back to: if I post them, it's going to be your fault.\n\nLynn wasn't choosing what Angela would publish. She was challenging Angela to do it. Angela still described the responsibility as belonging to Lynn.\n\nIt's the kind of moment that tells you something about the way these disputes worked. An action is described as a response to being pushed. The person on the receiving end is told they caused it.\n\nAnd there was another word in that exchange—*discovery*. Angela was talking about a legal process, as if the receipts she collected were already headed toward a courtroom. She spoke like that elsewhere, too.\n\n[ARCHIVAL 18 — ANGELA | *Petty Space*, September 8, 2026 | source **11:45–15:10**]\n\n> Because then I'll flip that uno, flip reverse, and have your ass serve, file a motion for discovery, put everything on fucking record, and it will be public information. Test me. I'm not worried. Test me.\n\n[LOGAN]\n\nAngela's explanation was that she had been threatened, harassed, and silenced, and that putting information into legal proceedings would help her answer those attacks. That was how she framed it. But threatening to put somebody's information on the record and actually having a legal case are two different things.\n\nLynn's story doesn't end here. We'll return to her, because later in the same broadcast she talks about losing businesses and trying to hold on to the part of herself that wanted to help people.\n\nFor now, the important thing is that I was beginning to have my own version of this conflict. And one of the reasons was the same name Lynn kept mentioning: Oor.\n\n---\n\n# CHAPTER FOUR — THE FRIEND IN THE MIDDLE\n\n[LOGAN]\n\nI started co-hosting Spaces with people Angela didn't trust. Oor was one of them. In my view, inviting somebody onto a stage or co-hosting a conversation didn't mean I endorsed every awful thing that person had said. Angela saw it differently. She believed people were platforming her harassers and helping them continue.\n\nThat disagreement was real. And once it became personal, she began speaking about me very differently.\n\nThere was someone else caught between those versions of events: Sav.\n\nSav was Angela's friend before Sav and I ever started dating. They knew each other from TikTok. They had talked privately, bonded over their lives as mothers, and discussed Angela's experiences. Sav came to X because she wanted to help someone she believed was her friend.\n\nAngela herself described that history.\n\n[ARCHIVAL 19 — ANGELA | *Logan Black Unmasked*, September 18, 2026 | V3 locator `20260918_1MJgNbdaAPlGL.json`, `/segments/89`, **3144.38–3227.34 seconds**]\n\n> Sav was my friend from TikTok. Sav came to Twitter to help me analyze the psychological warfare tactics that were happening on spaces because she wasn't in any personal relationships with anybody on this app. So no personal connections.\n\n[LOGAN]\n\nThen Sav and I got to know each other and started a relationship. Now two people she cared about were arguing with each other. She was hearing things from Angela that I didn't agree with, and things from me that Angela didn't agree with. It wasn't an easy position, and Sav didn't always handle it perfectly. Neither did I.\n\nWhen Sav and I argued, she talked to Angela about it. She sent screenshots of private conversations. She shared information about my life. She wasn't an outsider being fed a story in secret; she was a participant in a messy friendship and a messy relationship.\n\nI think that matters. If I leave that out, the rest of what happens sounds too neat. It wasn't neat.\n\nHere's one thing Angela said directly to Sav on September 8. This is after the conflict between all three of us had become public, but the words matter because they describe what Angela believed she owed a friend.\n\n[ARCHIVAL 20 — ANGELA ADDRESSING SAV | *Hook Line Sinker*, September 8, 2026 | `Hook_Line_Sinker_-_How_Psychological_Operations_Reel_Us_In_transcript (2).txt`, **35:05–36:40**]\n\n> Of course. Anytime you want to say something. You're more than willing. And I'm never going to put you in a position where you have to choose between me and another person. I'll bring it to DM. And I'll express my emotions on why I feel the way that I do. But I do believe that people should have meaningful connections with anybody that they connect with.\n\n[LOGAN]\n\nThat's a reassurance. Don't choose between me and somebody else. We can talk privately. People should have meaningful connections.\n\nAnd yet in the same broadcast, Angela explained that once she found out Sav and I were involved, she had started withholding information from her.\n\n[ARCHIVAL 21 — ANGELA | *Hook Line Sinker*, September 8, 2026 | V3 locator `/segments/28`, **2239.57–2407.14 seconds**]\n\n> As soon as I found out. You were in a relationship. With Logan. I stopped telling you. About the shit. That I was clipping. Because you were emotionally invested. Did I not? Like. I'm not trying to be mean. But like. That turns into a liability. Especially when you're documenting truth.\n\n[LOGAN]\n\nThose comments don't mean Angela was pretending the entire friendship was genuine. It isn't that simple. But they do show how quickly the question of who Sav trusted became tangled with who she was dating.\n\nI want to go back to July, because a private message shows how intense the hostility toward me had become.\n\n[WRITTEN MESSAGE — READ BY LOGAN, CLEARLY NOT AN ARCHIVAL VOICE CLIP | Angela to Sav, July 15, 2026 | `angela  sav transcript.txt`, lines **2320–2324**; speaker name mistakenly rendered \"Sav\" in transcript, corrected and confirmed by the producer as **Angela speaking about Logan**.]\n\n> Like, I'm not even trying to be a bitch, but if that bitch doesn't leave me the fuck alone when I go in spaces, I'm going to ruin every single person that he cares about. Just because they didn't have the goddamn balls To get this motherfucker, to leave me the fuck. Alone when I'm clearly obviously fucking tired of dealing with his fucking immature bullshit\n\n[DON'T REPEAT THE THREAT. SHORT PAUSE.]\n\n[LOGAN]\n\nThat message was sent to Sav. Angela was angry with me. And her stated response wasn't limited to confronting me. She wrote about ruining the people I cared about.\n\nBy late July, Sav was questioning something else. Had she been brought into this community to help a friend, or was Angela now telling a different story about why she was there?\n\n[WRITTEN MESSAGE — SAV TO LOGAN | July 24, 2026 | source cited in V3: `Logan_Sav_Chat_Transcript.txt`, line 29059, **8:10:24 PM**]\n\n> apparently the goal was to come take you down?? News to fucking me.\n\n[LOGAN]\n\nSav was telling me that Angela had described a supposed plan involving me. That is Sav's account of what was said, not proof of what Angela intended when she first invited her over from TikTok.\n\nAnd a few days later, Sav admitted something that complicated her own part in the dispute. When she was furious at me over the people I was hosting with, she had encouraged Angela.\n\n[WRITTEN MESSAGE — SAV TO LOGAN | July 27, 2026 | V3 source `Logan_Sav_Chat_Transcript.txt`, line 33129]\n\n> It’s her opinion and mine. that’s why I gassed her up about it.\n\n[LOGAN]\n\nSo Sav wasn't only a friend caught in the middle. There were moments when she helped make things worse. And later, when she tried to correct things she'd said privately, Angela didn't necessarily accept the correction.\n\nSav continued to reject the suggestion that she'd approached me as part of a plan. In an August message she put it pretty plainly.\n\n[WRITTEN MESSAGE — SAV TO LOGAN | August 6, 2026 | V3 source `Logan_Sav_Chat_Transcript.txt`, line 38468, **7:26:22 AM**]\n\n> I’m not a honey pot and she didn’t say get close to Logan to get info. If anything she said this is my friend who has helped me a ton already this is who to stick by but don’t fall in love with him.\n\n[LOGAN]\n\nThat's the picture Sav gave me. She had come to help Angela. Then she fell for me. Then she became part of arguments that were already tearing friendships apart.\n\nI can tell you what I believed at different points. I can't tell you Angela's unspoken plan from the beginning. And I won't pretend that Sav and I were having a perfect relationship while all this was happening.\n\nWhat I can tell you is that by September, things Sav shared as private conversations were about to become material for a public audience. And it happened in a way that leaves no doubt Angela knew she was publishing them.\n\n---\n\n# CHAPTER FIVE — FOUR AT A TIME\n\n[DROP ALL MUSIC. RETURN TO THE ROOM FROM THE OPENING MONTAGE, BUT START AT THE BEGINNING OF THE SOURCE BROADCAST.]\n\n[LOGAN]\n\nSeptember 8, 2026. Angela opened a Space with the title *Petty Space — Addressing the Men Who Provoked Me With My Dead Baby*.\n\nThe title is important. Angela said her actions were a response to remarks made about the loss of her child in a Space involving Oor and me. Her anger about those remarks was real. I say I intervened when those comments were made; I didn't endorse them. The broader conflict had already been public for weeks.\n\nBut on September 8, Angela made a choice about what to do next. She began posting private material.\n\n[ARCHIVAL 22 — ANGELA | *Petty Space*, September 8, 2026 | source **00:04–00:42**]\n\n> And now, let's have a little bit of fun in the comments section down below. I'm gonna be posting a series of screenshots that, um... Well, nobody wants to go out, so fuck it. But let's post this all on here, because, you know, apparently... This is the only way that we can get the truth out there as if I expose it.\n\n[LOGAN]\n\nThose screenshots concerned the private relationship between Sav and me. Angela said she believed they showed how I'd treated Sav. I reject her characterization. I also know the temptation here is to spend the next half hour going through private fights between two people who were dating. That's not the story I'm trying to tell.\n\nBecause regardless of which side of those arguments you're on, something else was happening in that room. Private things one friend gave another were being put before an audience. And Angela was narrating the process.\n\n[ARCHIVAL 23 — ANGELA | *Petty Space*, September 8, 2026 | source **01:53–02:21**, REPRISE SHORTER THAN PROLOGUE]\n\n> Alright, here's the next four screenshots posted down below. We're gonna do it in increments of four.\n\n[LOGAN]\n\nIn increments of four. Not one document released in a moment of confusion, but batches of screenshots presented while the room listened. She went on to say she had much more.\n\n[ARCHIVAL 24 — ANGELA | *Petty Space*, September 8, 2026 | source **11:45–15:10**, SELECT NONCONTIGUOUS LINES ONLY AT CLEAN SOURCE BOUNDARIES]\n\n> I will hold the rest until your response. Because apparently you're already crying about it now. Fucking funny.\n\n[EDIT — CONTINUE LATER IN THE SAME ORIGINAL TURN.]\n\n> And so if he wants to paint me as the big bad wolf, I'll share every fucking DM we've ever talked about going all the way back to 2023 in the Discord. And even the ones where you've edited your messages. Because like I told you, I screenshot in real time.\n\n[LOGAN]\n\nThat second part wasn't about screenshots Sav had handed over from our relationship. It was about private messages between Angela and me—from years when I was helping her. And now she was discussing their potential release as part of our public conflict.\n\nThere's that February recording again. The screenshots for a rainy day. The thing I barely noticed when I thought she was speaking about someone else.\n\nThe significance isn't that every note she ever took was meant to hurt somebody. The significance is that by September she was saying, on a live microphone, that she could publish years of our private conversations depending on how I responded.\n\nHer explanation matters here too. In another broadcast that day, she said she had changed her opinion of me because of messages Sav sent her about our relationship.\n\n[ARCHIVAL 25 — ANGELA | *Hook Line Sinker*, September 8, 2026 | original transcript `Hook_Line_Sinker_-_How_Psychological_Operations_Reel_Us_In_transcript (2).txt`, **55:03–57:47**]\n\n> And it wasn't until he had a relationship with my friend Sav, who was just in here, that I switched my opinion on him for the simple fact of what I witnessed on how he talks to her. And that's what he's upset about is that she has sent me screenshots of their conversations so that I can prove the abusive tendencies.\n\n[LOGAN]\n\nAngela says she was standing up for Sav. There are serious accusations about me in that recording, and I'm not asking you to pretend you didn't hear them. But what she believed about my relationship doesn't answer a separate question: whether Sav agreed to have her private messages made public.\n\nTwo days after *Petty Space*, Sav was trying to get the screenshots taken down.\n\n[WRITTEN MESSAGE — SAV TO LOGAN | September 10, 2026 | V3 source `Logan_Sav_Chat_Transcript.txt`, line 55892, **6:39:48 PM**]\n\n> I don’t know what else to do I’m trying to get her to delete shit and then I’m done talking about it with her.\n\n[LOGAN]\n\nAnd then there is a message from a later exchange between Sav and Angela that, to me, gets right to the heart of their friendship.\n\n[WRITTEN MESSAGE — SAV TO ANGELA | `Fallout Among Former Friends.txt`, line **43**. Absolute date not established in compiled source.]\n\n> Yeah at the end of the day you were a friend that used what I sent to you as a FRIEND against me.\n\n[BRIEF SILENCE.]\n\n[LOGAN]\n\nYou can hear all the complexity in that sentence. Sav is the person who sent information to Angela. She's acknowledging that. Her objection is to what the friend receiving it went on to do.\n\nAnd here is why that distinction matters. When Sav challenged one specific allegation Angela made about me, she wasn't disputing the entire history of their friendship. She was correcting a specific account of how a photograph got from one person to another.\n\n---\n\n# CHAPTER SIX — THE STORY A PHOTOGRAPH BECAME\n\n[LOGAN]\n\nOn September 15, Angela made another public statement about me. This time it concerned a photograph of Lynn.\n\n[ARCHIVAL 26 — ANGELA | *Super Spy Tea Time Red String Therapy, Part 4*, September 15, 2026 | V3 locator `20260915_1qGvvebNOARGB.json`, `/segments/234`, **9403.64–9412.86 seconds**]\n\n> Logan, stop sending women's nudes around the app. There's no reason for me to get women's nudes at 930 in the fucking morning on a fucking Monday before I've even smoked weed.\n\n[LOGAN]\n\nHere's my account of that particular photograph. Lynn had publicly posted an image of herself. Sav asked me to show her that post. I sent it to Sav, and Sav forwarded it to Angela. I dispute the claim that this was me distributing private nude photographs around the community.\n\nThe important thing isn't that I'm giving you my version and asking you to take my word for it. It's that Sav—the person who had asked me for the image—addressed the same point directly with Angela in writing.\n\n[WRITTEN READING — SAV TO ANGELA | `Fallout Among Former Friends.txt`, source lines **14–16**, SELECTED SENTENCES WITH EDITS BETWEEN SOURCE LINES; date unresolved]\n\n> Angela, you know that picture of Lin sent to me was because I asked him to show me the proof of it. not him just willingly spreading around this picture..\n\n[EDIT — MOVE TO SOURCE LINE 15.]\n\n> I was also sending you because I trusted you that it wouldn't come back that I sent it to you…..\n\n[EDIT — MOVE TO SOURCE LINE 16.]\n\n> Framing it as if he was going around spreading the picture just isn’t what happened…. Like, at all.\n\n[LOGAN]\n\nThat is Sav saying two different things. First, she asked me for that particular image. Second, she did not want the fact she'd passed it to Angela used against her. She wasn't writing a general defense of everything I'd ever done. She was correcting an account of one identifiable exchange.\n\nAngela responded with a broader allegation.\n\n[WRITTEN READING — ANGELA TO SAV | `Fallout Among Former Friends.txt`, source line **20**]\n\n> Thats old news apparently hes shared nudes a bunch with his close friends.\n\n[LOGAN]\n\nThat response moves away from the details Sav is discussing and asserts a wider history. The compiled conversation includes further allegations from Angela and references to other people who she says had supplied material. Those claims would need to be evaluated on their own terms. They do not change what Sav said about this specific photograph.\n\nThree days later, Angela publicly used the word *predator* about me—the clip you heard in the opening. I'm not treating that word as a proven description of me. I'm showing you the progression: an accusation in a public room, a correction from the person who forwarded the material, and the continued use of much larger allegations about my behavior.\n\nSav wasn't the only person asking what exactly Angela was trying to establish. In that same compiled exchange, she challenged the purpose of the escalating accusations.\n\n[WRITTEN READING — SAV TO ANGELA | `Fallout Among Former Friends.txt`, source line **63**, SELECT FIRST QUESTION ONLY AS ONE CONTINUOUS SENTENCE]\n\n> Angela what is the goal here.....? are we going after your voice being taken or something else entirely? What exactly is your goal here with this stuff? where is the evidence for any of it?\n\n[LOGAN]\n\nThat is a different Sav from the person who admitted she'd been encouraging Angela over my arguments with Oor. And that change matters. Her position wasn't fixed; it was changing as she saw what the conflict was becoming.\n\nNow I want to take you back a little earlier on September 15—before Angela made that accusation about the photograph. Because something she said in the very same broadcast may be the most revealing moment of this whole story.\n\n---\n\n# CHAPTER SEVEN — THE LINE SHE SAID SHE WOULDN'T CROSS\n\n[NO MUSIC. ORIGINAL SEPTEMBER 15 ROOM TONE.]\n\n[LOGAN]\n\nRemember Urs, the listener who thanked Angela for standing up for him? I told you we'd return to that moment. Immediately after he thanked her, Angela talked about the archive she'd collected.\n\nShe explained that some material should stay private, even when people wanted access to it. Here are her words.\n\n[ARCHIVAL 27 — ANGELA | *Super Spy Tea Time Red String Therapy, Part 4*, September 15, 2026 | V3 locator `20260915_1qGvvebNOARGB.json`, `/segments/159`, **6431.81–6492.36 seconds**; follows Urs segment 158 in the original recording]\n\n> because I have a private discord of evidence that I've collected from just, like, the abuse that I've witnessed. And I've never added anybody in there, even though a lot of people have wanted in there. Just because some of the evidence and stuff I've collected could be weaponized to hurt other people. And I don't feel like that is the right way to handle it. I've been tempted, not even to lie. But it's just the wrong way to go about it.\n\n[LET THE FULL END OF THE STATEMENT LAND. SILENCE.]\n\n[LOGAN]\n\nThere it is. In Angela's own words, she understands that releasing private material can hurt people. She says that's why she kept an archive closed, and why she hadn't let others into it.\n\nWhat makes this recording important isn't that I've caught her saying something bad. It's that she's saying something reasonable. Something I'd agree with: having access to private information doesn't automatically mean you should distribute it.\n\nThe timing is what stays with me.\n\nShe says this on September 15. One week after *Petty Space*, when she'd been releasing private relationship screenshots in batches and discussing what else she might publish. Later that same September 15 broadcast, she publicly made the accusation about Lynn's photograph.\n\nMaybe in Angela's mind those situations were different. She has repeatedly said she believed she was responding to people harming her or Sav. That's her position. And context matters.\n\nBut the tension is still there. She can state the danger of weaponizing private information with complete clarity. The question is how she decides when that principle applies.\n\nA few days later, she described a moment when she had abandoned restraint.\n\n[ARCHIVAL 28 — ANGELA | *Logan Black Unmasked*, September 18, 2026 | `LOGAN_BLACK_UNMASKED_-_WEAPONIZING_WOMEN_ON_UFO_X_transcript (3).txt`, **01:04:12–01:05:11**]\n\n> I didn't weaponize the information. I sat on it until I was poked and poked and poked and poked and then slapped around. Then I said, fuck it. I threw it all in the fuck it bucket\n\n[LOGAN]\n\nThat's her explanation for the turn she took. The information wasn't being used until she felt she'd been pushed too far.\n\nAnd this is where the story moves beyond me. Because when Sav started objecting to what Angela was doing, the argument didn't stay confined to the messages and voices on X.\n\nIt moved into their families, their personal lives, and a kind of fear that's a lot harder to close an app on.\n\n---\n\n# CHAPTER EIGHT — WHEN IT LEAVES THE APP\n\n[LOGAN]\n\nSeptember 16, 2026. In a written group conversation, Sav was objecting to what was happening. Angela responded sharply, and then referred to a private video and Child Protective Services.\n\nI want to be precise about this. The messages show what Angela said. They do not establish which agency ultimately received material, what anyone investigated, or what an agency concluded. But the words are important because of when they were used: during an argument with somebody she'd called a friend.\n\n[WRITTEN READING — ANGELA TO SAV, TWO SEPARATE MESSAGES | September 16, 2026 group conversation; V3 source `Angela Gemini Conversation.txt`, lines **7896** and **7900**]\n\n> If you want me to hold the fuck back, shut the fuck up, you dumb bitch\n\n[EDIT — LATER MESSAGE IN SAME GROUP CONVERSATION.]\n\n> I'm not canceling anything do you understand and when c p s gets hold of that video? Because of the proper mandatory reporter that I sent it to, that's not my issue. Fuck off\n\n[TWO SECONDS SILENCE.]\n\n[LOGAN]\n\nGo back for a second to how they met. Two mothers talking about their lives, trying to help each other through difficult things. And now one is telling the other to shut up while invoking child-welfare authorities.\n\nThere was also a police welfare check involving Sav. Angela described actions around Sav as concern for her safety; there were other people attempting to support Sav as well. I'm not going to pretend the messages alone tell us why every call or visit occurred. What they do capture is how far the relationship had deteriorated.\n\nOn September 18, Sav spoke publicly about the use of private information and what she said was happening to the people around her.\n\n[ARCHIVAL 29 — SAV | *Angela Maggard Fan Club*, September 18, 2026 | `Angela_Maggard_fan_club_transcript (2)(1).txt`, source around **02:51:04–02:53:33**, V3 attribution Speaker 12]\n\n> none of these, like, uh, screenshots should be shared. Any of these any of these personal information, like, and doxing and sending us just court stuff and any of that type of stuff is just it's just taking it way, way, way too far.\n\n[LOGAN]\n\nShe made a longer statement in that broadcast about a friendship becoming a source of conflict in her actual family life.\n\n[ARCHIVAL 30 — SAV | *Angela Maggard Fan Club*, September 18, 2026 | V3 locator `20260918_1AxRnZMeZNYxl.json`, `/segments/693`, **10095.89–10199.48 seconds**]\n\n> Like, first off, everything that was said, um, was obviously personal, deeply personal information that was kind of weaponized, uh, against me and you. I feel like, um, um, coming from a place that, like, you know, where where that came from was, you know, genuinely a friendship type thing. Right? And, um, it's just really unfortunate to see the turn of events and the way that, um, people that have only tried to ever help Angela, um, are being weaponized because she thinks that, like, there's some type of operation or, like, plot to take her down or steal her voice or not give her any room to speak when, um, I'll be the first one to say that, like, I said a million times that we you know, everything that was going on, we could have handled a lot differently. And, um, I just don't think that it's worth, you know, contacting people's families, um, people's children, people's exes, people's, you know, people's real lives, shit that hits, like, real life and can fuck people's whole shit up, which is kind of what's happening to me and definitely for sure Logan.\n\n[LONGER PAUSE THAN USUAL.]\n\n[LOGAN]\n\nSomething important happens in that clip. Sav doesn't say she played no part. She acknowledges that things could have been handled differently. And then she draws a line: whatever people are arguing about online, she says, it shouldn't reach their children, relatives, and exes.\n\nA woman who goes by Skittles describes a separate experience that sounds disturbingly familiar. She says she tried to take a call with Angela to calm a conflict, and then began getting repeated unwanted contact.\n\n[ARCHIVAL 31 — SKITTLES | *Angela Maggard Fan Club*, September 18, 2026 | V3 source line 385, broad **45:02–47:40**]\n\n> You say you're gonna take a phone call with her because you're like, okay. Let's we don't want, like, war. Like, let's try to have peace. And then she just calls and calls and calls and calls and calls, like, so much to the point. You have to block her on every avenue on the back end.\n\n[LOGAN]\n\nSkittles also says child-services workers and then police came to her home, and she blames Angela for making those contacts. I can't determine from the recordings alone who placed those calls. What you can hear is what Skittles says the repeated visits did to her.\n\n[ARCHIVAL 32 — SKITTLES | *Angela Maggard Fan Club*, September 18, 2026 | V3 source line 377, broad **42:50–44:57**]\n\n> I've been swatted. And when I say swatted, I mean, like, she's called child services. They show they showed up once a month for five months in a row, and then the sixth month, she called the cops. So I had five months in a row child services showing up on my door. And the sixth month, it was the cops. And it was only one cop that showed up, but still, they're on my property. You know? Like, fuck you. I got nervous to take my fucking son to school. You know? It it's just you know?\n\n[LOGAN]\n\nThink about the detail she gives there. Taking her son to school—an ordinary part of the day—had become something she was nervous about. She also says a daughter had to change her phone number after family members were contacted.\n\n[ARCHIVAL 33 — SKITTLES | *Angela Maggard Fan Club*, September 18, 2026 | V3 source line 419, broad **50:26–51:51**]\n\n> she called my ex husband. She called my firstborn daughter. My firstborn daughter had to change her fucking phone number.\n\n[LOGAN]\n\nThese are accounts by the people who say they experienced those consequences, not an independent determination about every call. I want their words in this story because they show what the conflict felt like when the microphone went off.\n\nBut there is another person who captures the danger for people who are already vulnerable before they ever enter one of these rooms. His name is Sine.\n\n---\n\n# CHAPTER NINE — THE PEOPLE WE SENT HER\n\n[LOGAN]\n\nSine hosted conversations where people opened up about difficult experiences. He believed Angela could help some of them. So when somebody needed a person to talk to, he says he pointed them in her direction.\n\nLater, speaking in a public Space, he sounded like somebody trying to make sense of the consequences of his own judgment.\n\n[ARCHIVAL 34 — SINE | *Angela Maggard Fan Club*, September 18, 2026 | source line 511, broad **57:51–58:56**]\n\n> Uh, there's a lot of people that I'll meet that'll come in my rooms when we're discussing this. Uh, these are people that have already been through plenty. You know? And if somebody asks me if they can get help from someone and I send them in her direction and then she turns these people into a new target. And it's like, I have only realized that she was doing this only just recently, and I've sent people in her direction numerous times, and I feel incredibly fucking guilty now.\n\n[DON'T ADD MUSIC.]\n\n[LOGAN]\n\nI recognize that feeling. Not because his situation and mine are identical, but because I used my own credibility to support Angela. I brought her onto my stage. I told people she deserved to be heard. I thought I was doing the right thing.\n\nWhen you're trying to help someone, you don't usually imagine you're giving them access to people who may later regret trusting them. You're thinking about the person in front of you who says they need help.\n\nSine is describing his belief that some of the people he referred became targets. That doesn't establish the details of every person's experience. It does establish his regret. And it's one of the reasons the story can't stop with whatever Angela said about me.\n\nAnother woman, Glow, described allegations involving a photograph of herself with her baby and information about her family being spread online. Angela disputed responsibility for posting that specific photograph and said another woman had posted it.\n\n[ARCHIVAL 35 — GLOW | *Angela Maggard Fan Club*, September 18, 2026 | V3 source line 1283, broad **01:47:52–01:48:20**]\n\n> she created that group chat with an account called detective Zaddy. And it sounds funny, but it really wasn't because she she did that in order to dox my, uh, uh, baby anonymously, but then she moved on to put it on her actual page and do it from her name.\n\n[ARCHIVAL 36 — ANGELA, HER RESPONSE | *Logan Black Unmasked*, September 18, 2026 | source window **12:56–19:22**]\n\n> Glow baby's gonna speak in that space. She doxed my baby. First of all, no. I did not. Chrissy posted a photo from your Facebook account. Was it wrong? Absolutely.\n\n[LOGAN]\n\nThat is a disputed claim, and the distinction matters. I can't turn Glow's attribution into an admission by Angela. In the same broadcast, though, Angela acknowledged a separate act concerning another person she'd been fighting with. She said she sent a photograph of the front door of that person's house into a group chat, while maintaining that the person had threatened her family.\n\n[ARCHIVAL 37 — ANGELA | *Logan Black Unmasked*, September 18, 2026 | source window **12:56–19:22**]\n\n> So, yes, I doxed the leader of that racist group chat. I did. I sent him the fucking front door the photo of his front door of his house. I in the group chat, not publicly,\n\n[LOGAN]\n\nIt's that last distinction she makes—*in the group chat, not publicly*—that tells you how differently people can draw the line around a private life.\n\nI've spent a lot of time on X. I've heard plenty of people accuse each other of being awful. I've heard threats made as jokes, and jokes repeated as threats. I know how easily a Space becomes a fight.\n\nBut these accounts aren't memorable because people yelled online. They're memorable because they describe the moment somebody's ordinary life gets pulled into it: a child, a family member, an address, somebody who never joined the argument.\n\nAnd that brings me back to Lynn.\n\n---\n\n# CHAPTER TEN — WHAT LYNN STILL HAD LEFT\n\n[LOGAN]\n\nAt the beginning, Lynn was the person trying to get Angela to agree to a truce. Somebody who said she didn't even know Angela that well, who wanted to support people she liked without being told she was funding somebody's harassment.\n\nI have described additional contact involving people connected to Lynn outside X, including her husband and a funding board. Those details come from my account; Lynn's recorded statement about losing businesses does not, by itself, establish why those businesses were lost. I don't want to confuse those two things.\n\nWhat Lynn says in the recording is still worth hearing, almost in full, because of the way she talks about what she'd given.\n\n[ARCHIVAL 38 — LYNN | *Who or What has Ruined UFO X Spaces* | V3 source line 1357, broad **01:54:06–01:54:53**]\n\n> guys, I'm not kidding you, like, it's still like a loss, you know? I don't wanna— I would never wanna take anybody down. I hope we can move on. Lessons learned. I don't mean ill will. I really don't. I am who I say I am. I am— yeah, I'm, I'm definitely wounded from the whole thing. I think I could have handled that way better than I handled it, and I lost the businesses anyways, so that's fine. I'm not gonna have much more to give at all anymore. That's okay too. But what I have had to give while I've been here, I, I don't, um, I don't regret.\n\n[ALLOW ORIGINAL ROOM SOUND TO FALL AWAY NATURALLY. THREE SECONDS SILENCE.]\n\n[LOGAN]\n\nThere's something I admire in that answer. She's not saying she handled everything right. She's saying she doesn't want to become somebody who hurts people because she got hurt.\n\nAnd it's easy to lose that part of the story if all we pay attention to is the loudest accusation. We stop hearing people as people. We hear a username, an enemy, somebody on a side. We forget that somebody can get up from an X Space and still have to go to work, take a child to school, explain a phone call to a relative, or figure out what to do when something private gets passed around.\n\nThat is what this story has forced me to think about. Not whether Angela and I will ever be friends again. That isn't the question. Not whether every person in these rooms behaved perfectly. We didn't.\n\nIt's whether the people who trusted her understood what might happen to their words when the relationship changed.\n\nAnd the thing is, Angela herself has offered an answer about what people owe each other when they're going to hold somebody accountable.\n\n---\n\n# EPILOGUE — IN HER OWN WORDS\n\n[NO MUSIC. NARRATION CLOSE-MIC, NEUTRAL.]\n\n[LOGAN]\n\nI still remember the person I defended. I can hear her in the recordings. I understand why somebody like Urs thanked her. I understand why Sine sent people her way. I understand why Sav thought she was talking to a friend. I was one of those friends.\n\nThe public accusations against me are part of what brought me to make this documentary. But listening through all of this changed the question I wanted to ask. It wasn't just, *Why did Angela say those things about me?*\n\nIt was: *What happens to people when the information they share in trust becomes material in a conflict?*\n\nSome things in these recordings are clear. We hear Angela describe saving conversations and making copies when a chat restricts screenshots. We hear her say she's still taking notes while she still cares about people. We hear her publicly announce the release of private screenshots. We hear the people who knew her explain how their relationships changed.\n\nOther things are contested. And those distinctions don't weaken the story. They're part of telling it accurately.\n\nIn February, before most of the events you've heard about here, Angela made a point about accountability. She was speaking about the responsibility of people who want to hold other people to account. I think it deserves the last word.\n\n[FINAL ARCHIVAL 39 — ANGELA | *Entry Level Improv and Music from the Beyond*, February 16, 2026 | V3 locator `20260216_1djxXNkreeNGZ.json`, `/segments/1635`, **21152.77–21190.83 seconds**]\n\n> everybody makes mistakes. I make mistakes every single day. But do we own up to them? Do we admit it if we're wrong? Like, that's something that we have to do, especially if we're gonna be holding other people accountable. We have to be fully transparent with ourselves first.\n\n[RECORDING ENDS NATURALLY. HOLD SILENCE. NO FINAL MORAL. NO REPEATED TITLE ANNOUNCEMENT. END.]\n\n---\n\n## Production-only review notes (not spoken)\n\n1. **Archival integrity:** All marked archival passages were selected from the provided V3 manuscript and/or accessible original text transcripts. Recordings were not auditioned; clip order, delivery, precise entrances and exits, and audio quality remain production-stage checks. Bracketed audio edit instructions do not authorize cutting within a sentence in a misleading way.\n2. **Source coverage:** The V3 file refers to several original transcript or JSON assets not present as raw files in the local attachment set, including the *Afterspace*, *Super Spy Tea Time* and *Who or What has Ruined UFO X Spaces* raw recordings. Their excerpts are preserved from V3's transcript-derived quotations and locators. Do not describe them as independently audio-verified in this draft.\n3. **July 15 attribution:** The local compiled `angela  sav transcript.txt` prints the message at lines 2320–2324 as \"Sav\". The producer has specifically confirmed this is a mislabeled message spoken/written by Angela concerning Logan. This proposed draft follows that explicit correction without representing the incorrect source label as proof.\n4. **External messaging:** The `Fallout Among Former Friends.txt` conversation is a compiled transcript that contains audio-attachment placeholders and relative time references (\"Yesterday\", \"Today\"). The absolute date of that exchange was not established here. Avoid dating its messages beyond what the source permits, and do not describe embedded audio notes as heard.\n5. **Potential exact-word cleanup:** The Skittles source quote in ARCHIVAL 32 should be checked against the raw broadcast; V3 transcribes its ending as \"You know? It it's just you know?\" with minor alternatives in other extractions. This is a transcription issue, not authorization to paraphrase the original recording.\n6. **Claims concerning children, agencies, and businesses:** The script deliberately distinguishes the recorded September 16 messages from conclusions about an agency's actions; Skittles's assertions about repeated visits from independent findings about who placed calls; and Lynn's recorded account of losses from Logan's account of their causes. Do not replace these distinctions with unsupported certainties.\n7. **Opening claims:** The prologue uses Angela's recorded allegations *about Logan* and immediately identifies them as disputed when Logan begins narrating. Keep enough original adjacent context to avoid implying allegations of conduct that her words did not actually make.\n8. **Sonic identity:** The three-note title motif is an original *direction*, not a generated track. Keep voice-led transitions dominant. No prescribed episode duration.\n\n**END OF COMPLETE PROPOSED MASTER DRAFT.**\n";

